# ToolTrack API — requests you can run from VS Code.
#
# Needs the REST Client extension (humao.rest-client, recommended in
# .vscode/extensions.json): each request gets a "Send Request" link above it.
# The extension keeps cookies between requests, so run the login once and every
# call below it is authenticated as that account.
#
# Start the server first: `npm run db:up && npm run db:schema:apply && npm run dev`.

@host = http://localhost:37411

# The login below uses these. Keep your real password out of this file — it is
# in the repository, and a password committed once is in the history for good.
# docs/api.local.http is gitignored and holds a ready-made login request;
# send it there and REST Client keeps the cookie for every request here.
@login_email = ola@example.com
@login_password = sekret1234

### Liveness. Never touches Postgres.
GET {{host}}/healthz

### What is running.
GET {{host}}/api/version

### Register. Always creates a viewer, whatever this asks for.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ola@example.com",
  "password": "sekret1234",
  "displayName": "Ola"
}

### Log in. The session cookie is kept by the extension from here on.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{login_email}}",
  "password": "{{login_password}}"
}

### Who am I, and what may I do? Render menus from `capabilities`.
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me

### The catalog.
GET {{host}}/api/items

### Search, filter and sort. An unknown condition is a 400; a broken limit is ignored.
GET {{host}}/api/items?q=makita&condition=needs_repair&sort=name&order=asc&limit=20

### The categories to offer in a filter, derived from the items themselves.
GET {{host}}/api/items/categories

### Add an item. Needs catalog.write, so a viewer gets 403 here.
POST {{host}}/api/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Młotowiertarka SDS",
  "category": "Wiertarki",
  "brand": "Makita",
  "model": "HR2470",
  "serialNumber": "12345-AB",
  "condition": "needs_repair",
  "notes": "Szczotki do wymiany"
}

### One card.
GET {{host}}/api/items/1

### Edit. Send only what changes; "" clears a field, omitting it leaves it alone.
PATCH {{host}}/api/items/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "condition": "good",
  "notes": ""
}

### Delete.
DELETE {{host}}/api/items/1

### Users. Needs users.manage, so only an admin gets past this.
GET {{host}}/api/users

### Promote someone to editor. You cannot change your own role.
PATCH {{host}}/api/users/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "editor"
}

### Change your own password. Ends every session, this one included.
PATCH {{host}}/api/auth/password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "sekret1234",
  "newPassword": "inne-haslo-9"
}

### Log out.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout
